# Question 1: descriptiveStats R Package

## Overview
A custom R package providing six statistical functions for descriptive analysis.

## Functions

### Central Tendency
- `calc_mean()` - Calculate arithmetic mean
- `calc_median()` - Calculate median value
- `calc_mode()` - Calculate mode (most frequent value)

### Spread/Dispersion
- `calc_q1()` - Calculate first quartile (25th percentile)
- `calc_q3()` - Calculate third quartile (75th percentile)
- `calc_iqr()` - Calculate interquartile range (Q3 - Q1)

## Features
- Full Roxygen2 documentation for all functions
- Comprehensive error handling for edge cases
- Unit tests using {testthat}
- Handles NA values appropriately
- Input validation with informative error messages

## Installation

```r
# Install from local source
devtools::install("path/to/descriptiveStats")

# Or load for development
devtools::load_all("path/to/descriptiveStats")
```

## Usage

```r
library(descriptiveStats)

# Example data
x <- c(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9)

# Calculate statistics
calc_mean(x)    # 5
calc_median(x)  # 5
calc_mode(x)    # 5
calc_q1(x)      # 3
calc_q3(x)      # 7
calc_iqr(x)     # 4
```

## Testing

